### 4. `src/components/SideMenu/styles.scss` (Modified)
- **Changes**:
  1. Added `white-space: nowrap;` to `.account-layout p` so menu labels ("Dashboard", "Investments", etc.) do not wrap or clip.
  2. Replaced fixed drawer height formula with `bottom: 0 !important; height: auto !important; z-index: 1100 !important; top: calc(var(--top-header-height, 0px) + --vih(64)) !important;`.
  3. Added mobile media query with `width: --vih(125) !important; min-width: --vih(125) !important;`.
- **Why**: Prevents the sidebar drawer from clipping at the bottom when zoomed, and stops menu item text from being cut off on smaller screens.

---

### 5. `src/components/Header/styles.scss` (Modified)
- **Changes**:
  Replaced hardcoded `width: 21.5% !important;` with `width: --vih(125) !important; min-width: --vih(125) !important;` inside mobile and tablet media queries.
- **Why**: Conforms with responsive viewport units (`--vih`) and ensures side drawer text remains readable across devices.

---

### 6. `src/layouts/styles.scss` (Modified)
- **Changes**:
  Dynamic viewport height adjustment using the custom `--app-zoom` variable:
  ```diff
  - min-height: 100vh;
  + min-height: calc(100vh / var(--app-zoom, 1));
  ...
  - height: 100vh;
  + height: calc(100vh / var(--app-zoom, 1));
  + max-height: calc(100vh / var(--app-zoom, 1));
  ```
- **Why**: When the page is zoomed (e.g. 120%), an element with `100vh` physically measures `120vh`, creating an unwanted second window scrollbar. Dividing by `--app-zoom` perfectly constrains the layout to the viewport height.

